  "query_preview": "/Monday through Friday/...\nHigh pressure aloft over the Four Corner region, and troughing \noff the British Columbia coast, will keep our area under \nsouthwesterly flow aloft. This troughing will help keep \nmonsoonal moisture south and east of our area, leading to hot, \ndry, and breezy conditions throughout the long-term period. Late\nin the week the Four Corners high will begin to shift west over\nthe Great Basin, allowing for a warming trend. Temperatures \nwill be near normal to start the coming week, before rising to \naround 5 degrees above normal come Wednesday.",
